    <div class="prose">
      <p>Most homeowners know their bathroom needs doing. They've known for a while. What tips them from "one day" to "let's get it booked" is seeing a proper transformation and the right person to do it. That's exactly what a good ad does: it turns a job they've been meaning to sort into an enquiry sitting on your phone.</p>

      <h2>What the ads bring in</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Full bathroom refits</li>
        <li>Wet rooms and walk-in showers</li>
        <li>Ensuites and cloakrooms</li>
        <li>Accessible and easy-access bathrooms</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why real footage wins</h2>
      <p>Bathrooms are all about the before-and-after. A dated, tired room turned into something clean and modern is a transformation homeowners can't scroll past. So we use <strong>real footage of your work</strong>, filmed on site or from finished jobs, never stock. Seeing your actual finish is what makes a homeowner trust you with a room they use every day.</p>

      <h2>What the funnel asks</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Is it a full refit, a wet room, or an ensuite?</li>
        <li>How many bathrooms, and roughly the size?</li>
        <li>What type of property, and the postcode?</li>
        <li>When are they looking to get it done, and the best number to reach them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>That turns a vague "thinking about our bathroom" into a real lead with the detail you need to quote it properly.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
